---
import Layout from '../layouts/BlogPost.astro';
---

<Layout
	title="About Me"
	description="AI & Data Engineering Consultant who loves deep hands-on coding with Python and ML"
	pubDate={new Date('2024-01-01')}
>
	<h2>About Me</h2>

	<p>
		I write code and think about machine learning. Currently doing AI & Data Engineering consulting at Deloitte in Germany (Frankfurt area), but honestly I'm just someone who likes building things with Python and figuring out how AI actually works.
	</p>

	<p>
		I did my bachelor's and master's in Computer Science at TU Darmstadt. My bachelor's thesis was on explainability in sentence transformers. My master's looked at query optimization using graph representations. Both came down to the same thing: what is the model actually learning? Where does it take shortcuts? Where does it break?
	</p>

	<p>
		That's still what I care about. I don't want to just throw AI at problems. I want to know if it's actually providing value, which is harder than it sounds, especially with GenAI.
	</p>

	<p>
		Day to day I work on infrastructure and backend systems. Lots of Python. Some Terraform and Ansible. I've got a Databricks Data Engineer cert and a Terraform cert, but I'm not claiming to be an expert at anything. I just know enough to get things done.
	</p>

	<p>
		Right now I'm trying to get better at Python engineering and learning Rust and Mojo on the side. Also getting into CUDA because if you're serious about ML you need to understand what's actually happening under the hood.
	</p>

	<p>
		I made this site to write about stuff I'm curious about or working on. Not trying to build a personal brand or whatever. Just want a place to think through things and share what I learn.
	</p>

	<p>
		Outside of work I like dancing with my fiancé. I also think way too much about how to be ambitious without becoming a hustle culture person. Still figuring that one out.
	</p>

	<p>
		That's pretty much it. I try to be honest and say what I actually think. If you want to chat about ML, Python, or anything else, feel free to reach out.
	</p>
</Layout>
